COMMON TRAPS
- ⚠️ Additivity vs. Vector Addition: Charge is scalar (algebraic sum); Electric Field/Force are vectors (vector sum).
- ⚠️ Mass change: Charging a body changes mass (e⁻ has mass!).
- ⚠️ Closed loops: Field lines never form closed loops (starts at +, ends at -).
- ⚠️ Potential vs. Charge: In conduction, charge flows until potentials are same, not necessarily charges.
- ⚠️ Dipole Force: F_net = 0 ONLY in uniform fields. In non-uniform fields, F_net ≠ 0.
- ⚠️ Gauss Law E: The E in ∮ E.dA is the net field from all charges, but flux only depends on enclosed charge.
- ⚠️ Medium: Using F = kq₁q₂/r² without dividing by K in a medium.
- ⚠️ 1/r² vs 1/r³: Monopole E ∝ 1/r² but Dipole E ∝ 1/r³.

